WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Hide your necks, here is Claes Bang!

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.100
Welcome here!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.320
Thank you!

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.920
We just saw a clip from Dracula.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.520
Yes. We did.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:28.480
What about you, do you think, made them give you that role?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.860
But ... I don't want to know that!

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.540
I don't want to know about it. If there's something in there that ... No.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.555
It should be said that

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.620
you needed a bit of makeup.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.440
Yes.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.220
And costume.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:46.100
Yes. This might be a little bit of a spoiler,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.300
but I'm really old in the beginning of this.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.100
Yes.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.440
200 years old.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.700
How much time did it take for you to become ..?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.520
It takes four hours.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.420
Was it uncomfortable?

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.100
Or was it easy?

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.100
With the makeup ...

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.580
When you were in the full Dracula outfit?

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.620
It was ...

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.540
What do you say in Swedish?

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.320
Nails.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.540
Nails. Yes, nails.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.660
There's teeth, there's contact lenses,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.040
there's about a kilo of plastic around this area.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.500
And you can't see anythi ng.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.320
When you're 200 years old, your eyes are very grey.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.440
So you have these grey ...

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.500
I couldn't see! And then

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.360
I had this cape and a candelabrum and shit!

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.600
I was very, very

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.840
scared that I would set fire to my hair.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.280
With this thing.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.960
What have you ...

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.920
I mean, you're from Copenhagen.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Yes.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.760
Can you remember when you were a child,

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.100
we were talking about Jonatan's fears as a child,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.640
what were you scared of when you were a child?

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.700
Everything.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.500
Everything. I was very scared when I was little.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.740
Can you remember a time when you were scared?

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.680
You said that you were scared when you were at home alone?

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.180
Yes.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.780
I was the same.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.720
It was scary.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.160
Just to walk in the door. «Hello?»

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.820
I didn't even go in, I just went somewhere else.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.240
Back to school or some place.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.180
I also think it's scary being in a room where I know that I'm the most competent person.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.200
So if something happens

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.040
it'll be up to me to fix it.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.260
I think that's an uncomfortable feeling.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.260
Aha. Okay.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:35.700
You have no confidence that you can do it?

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.480
Confidence isn't the problem. It's been proven through the years.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.000
Okay, so you want an adult in the room.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.060
Yes, exactly. Or just a very competent child!

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.660
A competent child.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.580
Are you a scared person? Are you ever scared?

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.240
Yes. I've been a coward my whole life.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.760
And I was scared of mean boys.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.660
Who were after me.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.880
Who were bigger than me.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.660
And I was scared of drunk men.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.000
Drunk guys.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.200
Yes, I was very ...

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.260
And as a child, I was often walking around the city.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.420
And when I saw a drunk man

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.880
I walked ...

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.380
I was completely sure that he would say something to me, or do something.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.000
And I thought it was horrifying.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.580
What are you scared of today?

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.620
Drunk men.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.480
You're doing quite well.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.220
One of the reasons for that is a movie called The Square.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.920
Which Ruben Östlund, the Swedish director, did.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:40.760
Yes.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.440
And you've praised Ruben Östlund

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.880
on every possible occasion.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.080
But working together wasn't completely unproblematic?

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:55.080
No, but a thing like that is never unproblematic, it will never be.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.840
But I ...

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:01.180
I'm extremely proud of that movie, I'm extremely proud of

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.340
the fact that I could do what he needed for his film.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.800
But, if you're completely honest,

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.480
how sick could you get of him?

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:12.260
Ah, I could get so sick of him.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.800
It's not even possible to describe!

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.600
I wanted to kill him!

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.360
You left the country ...

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.200
Yes.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.040
It was a weekend. My wife was doing a movie in Norway,

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.700
she was a makeup artist at that time.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.320
So I went to Norway.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.220
And then I was sitting there

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.400
hating Ruben Östlund.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.380
You spoke about that in an interview with L.A. Times.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.040
And then ...

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:44.720
It was quite obvious that you at that point didn't think that a Norwegian was going to ...

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.700
Read it?

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.720
... read it. Because you say that

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.340
«Norway is terrible!»

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:55.840
«I'm telling you. Norway is the worst!»

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.600
But you shouldn't go to Bergen if you're gonna experience Norway. It will rain there!

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.600
I'm sorry, Norway!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.100
I'm sorry.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.520
What do you mean by this, it's the best country in the world!

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:11.900
Is it the country or the people?

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.180
Everything. But ...

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.820
Oh my god!

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.340
I'm in trouble now!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:24.480
Because you were trying to describe how much you hated Ruben Östlund,

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.320
and you went to Norway, and even that was better than Ruben Östlund!

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.500
No, but it was like this,

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:35.940
it didn't go well for me, and then I was sitting there and

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.315
if I'm honest,

00:05:38.315 --> 00:05:41.565
I didn't know if he would

00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:43.925
want me to return to doing the movie.

00:05:44.305 --> 00:05:47.135
It didn't go well that day.

00:05:47.135 --> 00:05:49.875
So I was sitting in Norway thinking

00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:52.605
maybe I'll return to Gothenburg,

00:05:52.605 --> 00:05:55.560
where we were filming, and he will just be like «fuck off».

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.600
I didn't know.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.380
But what was the problem with Norway? That's what I'd like to know!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.440
It's not Norway's fault! If you lose ...

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.540
You're blaming Norway!

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.240
That's what I'm saying, it wasn't Norway's fault!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.260
It could be Norway's fault as well.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.080
All these things were happening.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:18.820
But you know how these things are. If you feel really bad

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.640
and then you're somewhere and you think «what the hell is this? I hate it!».

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.260
This film that we're talking about now,

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.500
it brought you to Cannes and it brought you to

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.400
the Palme d'Or award in Cannes.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.280
Yes.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:39.140
And this was an incredible award for ...

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.680
Do we really want to go there?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.880
Yes, because I want to know, what was it like for you to experience that?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.060
I became insane in Cannes.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.600
What happened?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.600
I lost my ...

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.980
I don't know. It was like this, we went to Cannes with the movie.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.180
And you can only win one award in Cannes.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.860
You can't win the prize for best movie and then win for best script too.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.180
You only get one.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.920
And then it was like this: Everyone liked this movie, and everyone

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.260
were saying that this was a really good movie,

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.940
«but you're not going to win, because it's too funny».

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.060
Everyone was saying

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:15.080
«if you get a call and they say that you should be there, you're going to win for something else».

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.280
So then I thought, «shit»,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:23.400
«maybe I'll get the award for best male actor, then!»

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.420
It began to ...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.420
Live in you?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.260
Yes!

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:28.480
And I ...

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.920
I started to believe the hype.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:36.560
Because I was reading in Variety , The Guardian, Hollywood Reporter,

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.560
they all said that I would win the award for best male actor.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.700
When we got the call on Sunday, I thought

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:43.760
«FUCK»!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.000
I'm going to get this!

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.620
And then we go there

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.595
and we're sitting there and they say

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.300
«and best male actor is» and I do this!

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.840
No, I didn't do that!

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.560
But it felt like it!

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:04.280
I've watched the show, and I'm like this.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.920
Clapping.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.520
Applauding Joaquin Phoenix.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.860
You can see clearly that I'm extremely disappointed.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.760
And then after about ten minutes,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.900
we win the big award.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:21.040
And then we're completely euphoric, everything is fantastic.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.060
And then ten more minutes pass, and it feels like

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.140
something's not quite right.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.500
«I think they may have made a mistake.»

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.720
Even though you had received the biggest award?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.660
Yes! I know!

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.400
And Ruben even said on stage that he shared the award with me!

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.080
Yes. It was ...

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:43.560
He doesn't mean that, you know.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.420
I was calling everyone ...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.200
Did you call everyone beforehand, all your old enemies, and tell them to go to hell?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:56.280
I called all my agents and said «what the hell is this?! I was supposed to get that award!»

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.460
And they were like «listen. This is really good.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.640
No one watches a movie because it has won

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.360
the prize for best male actor in Cannes

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:08.160
but everyone watches the Gold Palm winner!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.180
So this is very good for you, because you're great in the movie! Everyone will watch it.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.320
It will mean a lot of business.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.720
But it didn't feel like it?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:17.780
No. It didn't.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:20.500
So I called another agent. And another agent.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.080
And everyone said the same thing.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.120
And at this point I was really drunk.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.080
It's the biggest party you can ...

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.140
There's so much champagne, you can't even ...

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.920
It never ends.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.720
Fucking hell. Why am I telling this story?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.580
So I was really drunk and then

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.380
I see Ruben Östlund returning from the press conference.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.840
All the winners return. And I just think

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.440
«fuck you».

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.760
«I'm gonna hurt you.»

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.000
And after that, I knew that I had to go home.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:01.940
«I have to go home, because I've done crazy things while I was drunk.»

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.740
And I just saw myself walking over, trying to take this golden palm and just

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.160
steal half of it or something!

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:14.620
It wasn't good. So I said to my wife that we had to go home. And she said

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.240
«Are you an idiot?!»

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:23.720
«Just have a look around! There's David Lynch, there's this person, you can talk to everyone, and they've seen your movie.»

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.240
«They think you're great, what the hell!»

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.320
I said «I can't do it, I'm going to kill him!»

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.740
«I'm going to kill him!»

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:36.280
You would've gotten so many parts if you had killed him!

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.100
Everyone loves a crazy actor.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:42.220
In any other profession, you would've been fired.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.860
But in this one, you just would've become a  new Klaus Kinski!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.180
Just kill Ruben Östlund!

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:52.000
«I want him in my next film», I really think everyone would've said that!

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.100
Just kill him!

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.540
I'm actually happy I didn't do it.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:01.280
But when you were drunk and calling around, did you think ...

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.380
Was your goal to try to get them to redo their decision?

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:07.960
Were you thinking that ...

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.080
«We should be able to do something about this?»

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.000
Yes! «Can you call them?»

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:16.080
«Can we get everyone back in that big room?»

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.940
«There's been a mistake.»

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:20.420
«Did you think this through?»

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.140
«We've been doing some thinking ...»

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.320
Yes.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.220
I don't know what the hell I wanted.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.340
When you talk about it, I agree that it sounds completely absurd that you didn't win!

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.520
But we ended up leaving the place, and that was that.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:42.840
Claus, we began this conversation talking about an iconic character, Dracula.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:49.020
I thought I would finish by asking a question about another iconic character,

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.540
that soon has to find yet another actor to portray him,

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:54.860
James Bond.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.220
And I know that you're in ...

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.880
... what's it called ...

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.000
... the odds, or ...

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.040
The loop?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:08.020
A lot of people want you to get that question.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.460
Would you be able to do something new for that ...

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.160
You're renewing Dracula, would you be able to renew James Bond?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:19.340
As with Dracula, and it would be the same with Bond, I wouldn't do something just because

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.180
it's called Bond or Dracula.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.740
I want to read scripts.

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:26.940
But if they call and ask you «do you want to play James Bond» you don't ask for a script!

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.920
Hell yeah, I will!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.200
They could call you?

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.420
I don't have to see any script!

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.400
But then you'll regret it!

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.560
How about you, would you say yes to playing Bond?

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.640
Yes, but I would've half-arsed it.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.680
To be on the safe side.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:52.640
But I'll promise you this, if I get the Bond part, there will be phone calls from Bang!

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.920
Then it's all «there's been a mistake»!

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.420
But do you think you would be able to do it?

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.320
I have no idea.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.560
Have you ever looked in the mirror and said

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.140
«My name is Bond ...»

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.020
No.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.680
I've looked in the mirror and said «my name is Bang»!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.600
«My name is Bang. Claes Bang.»

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.180
It's very close!

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:23.440
It's close!

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.180
Thank you so much, Claes Bang, it's fantastic having you here!

